I completely agree.

I think the one of the biggest problem with the game as it stands now,
is it's overreliance in items.  The reason why every character looks
the same is because pretty much everyone wears same armor set (with
minor variations) with super-high armor class to make pretty much
everyone immune to regular physical damage from monster attacks,
everyone uses same kind of weapons, etcs.  They overwhelm most of the
other aspect of the game that makes classes unique (skill sets, etcs).


The only place you see diversions in characters are:

Strong magic or not

Two weapon or not

As you can see, they are skill based.  I would love to see the game
expand in that direction, and see that an expert polearm users are
*better off* using polearms enchanted up to +1, than using saver
enchanted up to +7, but basic skilled in saber, or something along that
line.

And expand on those.  I'd love to see expert weapon users being able to
generate extra effects out of the weapons used, something like
Jousting, multi-shots, backstabbing of rogues, etcs.

At the same time, I'd like to see more weapon customization other than
'Enchant them up to +6/+7'.  Something along the line of being able to
custom craft weapons that does something similar to artifact weapons.
Like adding Lightning Enchanted quality that does +d10 against monsters
that doesn't resist lightning...and be able to add that to the weapon
of your choice.  Lightning Spear, anyone?

So, what I'm suggesting is pretty fundamental change in the game
itself, so I suspect it'll never happen.  But that's what I'd love to
see happen.  

